--- a/tcg/tier3.c
+++ b/tcg/tier3.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1763 @@
+/*
+ * POMPPC tcg/0049 (x-tier3): the region compiler.  The captured TCG ops of
+ * the TBs of a region (include/tcg/tier3.h) become ONE LLVM function
+ *
+ *     const void *region(CPUArchState *env)
+ *
+ * which returns the host code to jump to (a TB, or the epilogue to go back
+ * to the main loop), like the goto_ptr of a TB.  Every TCG op is translated
+ * one for one; what changes is what TCG does between TBs and around its
+ * ops:
+ *
+ *  - the TB exits that go to another TB of the region (constant nip of a
+ *    goto_tb or of a lookup, or a return predicted from a bl of the region)
+ *    are branches; the exits that leave call helper_lookup_tb_ptr and
+ *    return its result;
+ *  - the guest registers (TCG globals) live in LLVM values (allocas that
+ *    mem2reg promotes); they are written back to env, those that may be
+ *    dirty only (a dataflow over the region), before a helper that reads
+ *    globals, on the slow path of a guest access, and at the region exits;
+ *    reloaded after a helper that writes globals;
+ *  - the head check of each TB (icount_decr) is kept only on the back edges
+ *    of the region (with the "region dead" flag), the guest access fast
+ *    path (softmmu TLB) is inlined, the slow path calls helper_*_mmu;
+ *  - where TCG would restore the guest pc from the host return address of
+ *    a helper that raises (cpu_restore_state), the region stores the pc of
+ *    the instruction in cpu->t3_pc first (accel/tcg/translate-all.c).
+ *
+ * A TB whose ops are not all translated here (vector ops, ppc_fp32, ...)
+ * is not taken in a region (tier3-capture.c.inc says why).
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
